From: triangleXIV <127415617+triangleXIV@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:22:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] feat(images): serve Gemini image models on the OpenAI
 images API

/v1/images/generations and /v1/images/edits now accept Gemini image
models (gemini-*-image, e.g. gemini-3.1-flash-image). The request is
converted to a native Gemini generateContent payload and executed
through the gemini handler surface, so every auth registered for the
/v1beta endpoint (API key, Vertex, AI Studio, Antigravity) serves the
OpenAI images API too; inlineData parts are converted back to OpenAI
images JSON (b64_json + usage from usageMetadata).

Parameter compatibility:
- OpenAI size (WxH) maps to imageConfig.aspectRatio (1024x1024 -> 1:1,
  1536x1024 -> 3:2, 1024x1536 -> 2:3, ...); ratio strings and
  square/landscape/portrait aliases pass through
- Gemini size tiers map to imageConfig.imageSize: explicit
  image_size/image_config.image_size, tier-sized 'size' values, or
  OpenAI quality semantics (low/standard -> 1K, medium -> 2K,
  high/hd -> 4K)
- Gemini-style aspect_ratio/image_size and image_config.{aspect_ratio,
  image_size} fields are honored and win over OpenAI spellings
- n>1 maps to generationConfig.candidateCount
- edits: input images (JSON image_url or multipart image[]/image files)
  become inlineData parts; masks are appended as additional input images

Streaming is intentionally not offered on this path: the upstream call
is non-streaming and the result is returned as plain OpenAI images JSON.
